WEBVTT

00:00:00.609 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.637 --> 00:00:03.950
Today, we are talking about waxing:

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:05.630
hair removal with wax.

00:00:05.967 --> 00:00:06.830
It looks simple:

00:00:06.932 --> 00:00:08.990
apply the wax, then pull it off.

00:00:09.262 --> 00:00:14.754
But in a spa, this is the service most likely to burn the client, break the skin,

00:00:14.704 --> 00:00:16.030
or leave red bumps,

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:16.910
if it is rushed.

00:00:17.339 --> 00:00:21.690
Done right, the client feels less pain, the skin is smooth and clean,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.310
and the client comes back.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.149
Something very common:

00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:29.554
the salon is busy, the wax pot is too hot, the therapist doesn't test it,

00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:32.028
and applies it straight to the client's leg.

00:00:32.457 --> 00:00:36.589
The client flinches, and there is a red, burning streak on the skin.

00:00:37.086 --> 00:00:38.429
Sometimes it is the opposite:

00:00:38.698 --> 00:00:43.069
the wax has cooled, the therapist pulls slowly, and pulls straight up.

00:00:43.426 --> 00:00:48.109
The skin is dragged along, and the next day there is bruising, and broken skin.

00:00:48.355 --> 00:00:51.229
Both mistakes can be avoided with a few small habits.

00:00:51.775 --> 00:00:53.802
There are two main kinds of wax.

00:00:53.974 --> 00:00:56.682
Soft wax, also called strip wax:

00:00:57.031 --> 00:01:01.002
apply a very thin layer, place a strip on top, then pull.

00:01:01.443 --> 00:01:05.482
This kind is fast, and suits large areas like legs and arms.

00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:07.722
Hard wax needs no strip:

00:01:08.071 --> 00:01:12.122
apply it thicker, wait for it to set, then grab the edge and pull.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.928
Hard wax grips the hair and sticks less to the skin,

00:01:15.878 --> 00:01:18.362
so it suits small areas with thin skin:

00:01:18.621 --> 00:01:21.402
underarms, brows, the upper lip.

00:01:21.688 --> 00:01:25.402
Every wax brand is different, so always read the brand's instructions.

00:01:26.015 --> 00:01:28.294
Temperature is the first safety issue.

00:01:28.626 --> 00:01:32.774
Each wax has its own working temperature, given in the brand's instructions.

00:01:33.029 --> 00:01:34.294
Don't just trust your eyes.

00:01:34.746 --> 00:01:38.059
Before every client, take a little wax with a new spatula,

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:40.534
and test it on the inside of your own wrist.

00:01:40.964 --> 00:01:44.214
Then test a small spot on the client's skin, and ask:

00:01:44.678 --> 00:01:45.814
does that feel too hot?

00:01:46.293 --> 00:01:49.734
The wax should be warm, and flow smoothly, like honey.

00:01:49.984 --> 00:01:51.734
Too hot, and it burns.

00:01:52.004 --> 00:01:55.414
Too cool, and it drags the skin, and hurts.

00:01:56.074 --> 00:02:00.500
The hair must be long enough for the wax to grip, usually about half a centimeter,

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.995
the size of a grain of rice.

00:02:02.406 --> 00:02:04.475
Too short, and the wax can't hold it:

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:07.835
if the client has just shaved, rebook in a few weeks.

00:02:08.171 --> 00:02:11.035
Too long, trim it first, so it hurts less.

00:02:11.608 --> 00:02:13.675
The skin must be clean and dry:

00:02:13.929 --> 00:02:16.555
no cream, no oil, no sweat.

00:02:16.974 --> 00:02:20.555
Wipe it clean with a pre-wax cleanser, as the brand instructs.

00:02:21.085 --> 00:02:23.852
Before waxing, always ask about medication.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:28.252
A client taking the acne medicine isotretinoin must not be waxed.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.252
If they have recently stopped, the usual wait is about six months:

00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:34.172
let the client ask their doctor.

00:02:34.751 --> 00:02:37.612
Retinoid creams, or exfoliating acids:

00:02:37.881 --> 00:02:40.012
don't wax the area where they are used;

00:02:40.279 --> 00:02:43.452
follow the wax brand's instructions, and the doctor's.

00:02:43.708 --> 00:02:50.812
After a recent peel or laser, on sunburn, broken skin, a cold sore, or a rash:

00:02:51.029 --> 00:02:52.252
don't wax that area.

00:02:52.899 --> 00:02:54.183
Varicose veins:

00:02:54.422 --> 00:02:55.383
don't wax over them.

00:02:55.773 --> 00:03:01.315
If the client has diabetes, or circulation problems, thin skin that bruises easily,

00:03:01.265 --> 00:03:02.903
or takes blood thinners:

00:03:03.172 --> 00:03:06.053
the skin heals more slowly, so be very careful,

00:03:06.003 --> 00:03:08.583
and advise them to ask their doctor first.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.263
We do not diagnose.

00:03:10.443 --> 00:03:11.783
If in doubt, don't.

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:15.463
The lesson on when not to treat a client covers this in detail.

00:03:15.977 --> 00:03:19.655
For a client waxing for the first time, with sensitive skin,

00:03:19.605 --> 00:03:21.227
or a history of allergies:

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.507
patch test first.

00:03:23.089 --> 00:03:28.187
Many waxes contain rosin, also called colophony, which some people are allergic to.

00:03:28.728 --> 00:03:32.589
Test a small patch in a discreet spot, usually the day before,

00:03:32.539 --> 00:03:34.187
or as the brand instructs.

00:03:34.463 --> 00:03:35.227
But remember:

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.507
no redness after a test is still not a guarantee.

00:03:39.127 --> 00:03:42.991
Now, the technique, and the most important thing is direction.

00:03:43.325 --> 00:03:46.271
Soft wax is applied in the direction of hair growth.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.991
The pull goes against the direction of growth.

00:03:49.255 --> 00:03:54.111
Pull very fast, decisively, close to the skin, almost parallel to it.

00:03:54.539 --> 00:03:55.871
Do not pull straight up:

00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:00.831
the skin gets dragged, bruises and breaks easily, and the hair tends to snap.

00:04:01.123 --> 00:04:06.204
In the underarm, hair grows in several directions, so divide it into small areas,

00:04:06.154 --> 00:04:08.191
each waxed in its own direction.

00:04:08.803 --> 00:04:12.592
Your other hand always holds the skin taut, right next to the strip.

00:04:13.064 --> 00:04:15.792
Taut skin hurts less, and doesn't get dragged.

00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:20.992
After the pull, press your palm on the waxed area right away, for a few seconds:

00:04:21.262 --> 00:04:22.992
the client feels much less sting.

00:04:23.545 --> 00:04:27.072
With soft wax, don't go over the same spot more than twice.

00:04:27.407 --> 00:04:29.632
If a few hairs are left, use tweezers;

00:04:29.855 --> 00:04:30.912
don't apply wax again.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.965
Hygiene in waxing has a golden rule:

00:04:34.136 --> 00:04:35.325
no double dipping.

00:04:35.896 --> 00:04:40.605
Once a spatula has touched the client's skin, it never goes back into the wax pot.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.485
Every time you take wax, use a new spatula.

00:04:44.066 --> 00:04:44.687
Otherwise,

00:04:44.637 --> 00:04:49.085
the wax pot becomes a way for bacteria to travel from one client to the next.

00:04:49.412 --> 00:04:52.285
Wax that has been taken out never goes back into the pot.

00:04:52.708 --> 00:04:56.605
Wear gloves, and use fresh bed paper, and single-use strips.

00:04:56.708 --> 00:05:01.405
Watch the hand hygiene lesson, and the lesson on tools after every client, again.

00:05:01.952 --> 00:05:04.217
This lesson covers the common areas:

00:05:04.324 --> 00:05:07.817
legs, arms, underarms, and brows.

00:05:08.246 --> 00:05:12.297
The client is always covered, with only the area being worked on uncovered.

00:05:12.804 --> 00:05:14.217
For the face and brows:

00:05:14.329 --> 00:05:19.577
use hard wax, in a very small amount, carefully, well away from the eyes.

00:05:20.085 --> 00:05:23.550
Intimate waxing is a separate technique that needs its own training,

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.257
and it is not part of this lesson.

00:05:25.911 --> 00:05:31.190
After waxing, slightly red skin, with a few small bumps at the follicles, is normal,

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.431
and usually goes within a few hours.

00:05:33.861 --> 00:05:34.711
Tell the client:

00:05:35.102 --> 00:05:40.793
for about the first day, avoid sunbathing, saunas, very hot baths or showers,

00:05:40.743 --> 00:05:42.551
and fragranced products,

00:05:42.581 --> 00:05:44.951
including deodorant after underarm waxing.

00:05:45.454 --> 00:05:49.111
If the wax brand has its own aftercare advice, follow the brand.

00:05:49.719 --> 00:05:52.807
Ingrown hairs are something clients often ask about.

00:05:53.315 --> 00:05:58.327
After a few days, exfoliate very gently, and moisturize regularly.

00:05:58.756 --> 00:06:00.647
No squeezing, no picking.

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:06.647
If the spot is swollen, painful, or has pus, advise the client to see a doctor.

00:06:07.076 --> 00:06:08.487
And if you do cause a burn:

00:06:08.726 --> 00:06:12.609
cool it right away under cool running water, for about twenty minutes,

00:06:12.559 --> 00:06:14.087
as in the incidents lesson.

00:06:14.594 --> 00:06:15.767
If the skin lifts:

00:06:16.019 --> 00:06:19.127
stop, don't wax that spot again, and write it down.

00:06:19.791 --> 00:06:20.508
Finally:

00:06:20.849 --> 00:06:23.548
the rules for beauty work differ from country to country.

00:06:23.933 --> 00:06:27.308
This lesson is training material, not a professional license.

00:06:27.856 --> 00:06:33.468
In the practice lesson, we will wax lower legs, underarms and brows, step by step.

00:06:33.812 --> 00:06:36.828
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:37.079 --> 00:06:37.948
See you next time.
